<title>SWEDEN: Iceland November airport cargo volumes up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Iceland November airport cargo volumes up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iceland's international airport at Keflavik handled 1,961 tonnes of freight in November, 15 percent more than in November 1995, Iceland's civil aviation administration said on Monday.</p>
<p>The administration published the following figures about airport activity for the month.</p>
<p>					     Nov 1996	 Nov 1995</p>
<p>KEFLAVIK INT'L AIRPORT</p>
<p> Cargo export (in tonnes)		1,321	    1,110</p>
<p>	 import				  640		596</p>
<p>	 Total				 1,961	    1,706</p>
<p> Mail export (in tonnes)		    59		 48</p>
<p>	 import				  129		147</p>
<p>	 Total				   188		195</p>
<p> Passengers				 68,168	   67,801</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
